# R8 keep rules for the release build. AGP combines every file in src/main/keepRules and passes them
# to R8, on top of the consumer rules the dependencies ship (kotlinx-serialization, Room, Hilt and
# ML Kit GenAI all carry their own).
#
# Only one thing in this app needs a rule of its own, and it is not obvious:

# Enum names are DATA here, not just identifiers. A document's kind and the engine that read it are
# stored in Room by name (`insight.kind.name`) and read back by matching that name against
# DocumentKind.entries. If R8 renames the constants, every row written by an earlier build stops
# matching: the mapper falls back to Unknown/Rules instead of crashing, which is worse — the archive
# would quietly lose what it knew about every document already in it.
-keepclassmembers enum com.hacybeyker.snapdoc.** {
    <fields>;
    public static **[] values();
    public static ** valueOf(java.lang.String);
}
